# LRAN W9 bench run (R9) - spec 6.6 PING over RF against /lib/lran-protocol/
# captured 2026-09-05
#
# note: two Heltec V3 on the bench, ~1 m apart, 3.0 dBi production antennas, test
#   point 0 (SF7, BW 125 kHz, CR 4/5, 915.0 MHz, conducted -9 dBm). This is a
#   PROTOCOL test, not a link test - the path is deliberately trivial so that any
#   fault is the codec, the fragmentation or the buffers, and not the RF.
#
# spec: LRAN-Protocol-Specification v0.7, 6.6 / 6.6.1 / 6.6.2 / 6.6.3 / 11 / 12.3 / 15.1
# firmware: firmware/range-test, role W9-INIT / W9-RESP (serial w / x)
#
# Run 1 is spec 6.6.1: a 202-byte echo, a frame of exactly 222 bytes, unfragmented.
# Run 2 is spec 6.6.2: the same echo at frag_chunk = 14, the full 15-fragment set.
#
# NOT a CSV. W9 emits console lines only, so capture.py reports "no CSV header seen"
# and exits non-zero on a completely successful run. That is expected here.
#
# --- INITIATOR (node 0xF0) ---
# W9 - spec 6.6 PING over RF, against /lib/lran-protocol/.
# node ids: initiator 0xF0 responder 0xF1 (spec 5.3 bench range - never a production node)
